# The vendored core2 patch is a byte-exact integrity fixture: its
# recorded checksum (vendor/core2/.cargo-checksum.json) covers the
# committed LF bytes, so Windows checkouts must NOT convert line
# endings. The rest of the tree follows the default autocrlf policy.
vendor/core2/** -text

# Release-manifest signature fixtures are byte-exact: the cosign
# signature and certificate cover the exact committed bytes, so
# Windows checkouts must NOT convert their line endings.
tests/fixtures/** -text
